# Tooltip

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A tooltip is a small box of text that appears next to a control when someone points at it or moves keyboard focus to it. Home Assistant uses tooltips to name icon buttons, such as the buttons in an overflow menu, and to explain items in settings screens.

You cannot add a tooltip to a dashboard card. There is no card or Markdown tag for it. This page tells you what Home Assistant does, so you know what to expect from its screens and what to write yourself. For visible help, see [Help / hint text](hint-text.html).

This page covers:

- Tooltip
  - `ha-tooltip`
  - `ha-help-tooltip`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

A tooltip has one box of text and an optional arrow. It is attached to a control, called the anchor, and opens above it unless there is no room. By default it opens when the pointer rests on the anchor for 350 milliseconds or when the anchor receives focus, and it closes 150 milliseconds after the pointer leaves or when focus moves away.

A help tooltip is a small question-mark icon. The tooltip text opens when you hover over it.

